.TH CYAML_TYPE_STR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_type_str \- return a string name for a node's type
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_type_str(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return a static string literal that names the type of node, such as
"CYAML_INTEGER", or "CYAML_UNKNOWN" for a type value that the function
does not expect.  It is useful in diagnostics and in test output.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A static null-terminated string, which the caller must not free.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_type (3)
